# Build context is the repo root; only the agent's own content belongs in it.
#
# A denylist rather than str-hermes-agent's deny-everything-then-allow, and the
# reason is what this repo holds: no verbatim guest data, no vault, nothing that
# must never reach a published image. What it does have is an active build
# window and files landing in it while this is being written, and under an
# allowlist a new tracked file is invisible to the build until somebody
# remembers to name it here. This is life-assistant-hermes-agent's shape, with
# MATE's own entries added. If this repo ever grows a directory of real user
# data, invert it.
.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.*

# The live agent token `plow-agents mint` writes beside compose.yml. The build
# context is this directory, so without this line it is reachable from a COPY.
plow-credentials

# `**/` is load-bearing: a bare `__pycache__` matches only the context root, and
# the ones that matter are under mate/ and under every skill's scripts/
# directory. A stray .pyc can also carry a value compiled before an edit --
# measured elsewhere, it survived a source revert and kept a test red.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[co]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache

# The plan cache Settings.cache_dir writes. A local run leaves fetched Overpass
# and OSRM responses here; baking one into a layer ships a frozen snapshot of
# somebody else's query results as if it were the agent's own.
.cache
**/.cache

# Local tooling and editor state. None of it is COPY'd, and all of it makes the
# context bigger and the layer hashes noisier.
.venv
venv
node_modules
.idea
.vscode
.DS_Store
.claude

# Tests run against the checkout, not inside the image: the image ships the
# mate package, not its test suite.
tests

# Documentation. README.md is what a judge reads on GitHub, not something the
# container needs.
README.md
REVIEW.md
docs
